# SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-P-2.0
#
# Colorlight i9 v7.2 — bring-up step 3, two pins.
#
# Both balls and both IO_TYPEs are colorlight_i9.lpf's, unchanged, and
# the provenance argument for them is written there in full. LVCMOS33 is
# no longer an assumption here: bank 6 measured 3.28 V on 2026-08-11, so
# the declaration matches the rail.
#
# Two constraints against two ports, which is the check: a stale LOCATE
# is skipped in silence (ecp5/lpf.cc:144), but the port it stopped
# covering then fails the build with "IO <name> is unconstrained in LPF"
# (ecp5/main.cc:287).
#
# clk25 is the only pin nextpnr is told about. clk_tx and clk_sys are
# PLL outputs and are constrained by what EHXPLLL's parameters say they
# are, which is the point of building this: the report has to show
# nextpnr constraining a 125 MHz domain that exists only if the PLL was
# elaborated as intended.
#
# WHAT THIS BUILD CANNOT SETTLE. Nothing here touches the PHY, the RGMII
# pads or bank 6's twelve Ethernet pins, so a working 1 Hz says the
# clocking is right and says nothing whatever about the receive path.
# That is step 4, and the delay value it needs is empirical: prjtrellis
# carries no timing characterisation of DELAYG or DELAYF at all.
#
# The FREQUENCY line is also the spelling check on clk25: a net that does
# not exist warns rather than passing quietly (common/kernel/basectx.cc:108).

FREQUENCY PORT "clk25" 25 MHZ;

LOCATE COMP "clk25" SITE "P3";
IOBUF  PORT "clk25" IO_TYPE=LVCMOS33;

LOCATE COMP "led_n" SITE "L2";
IOBUF  PORT "led_n" IO_TYPE=LVCMOS33;
